From: User <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] aarch64: accept() is accept4(fd, addr, len, 0)

__ASSUME_ACCEPT_SYSCALL is undefined for aarch64, so accept() issues
accept4(fd, addr, len, 0) (still a cancellation point), which Linux defines
to be accept.

The Android 13 (API 33) app seccomp policy allows accept4 but traps accept
with SIGSYS.
---
--- a/sysdeps/unix/sysv/linux/aarch64/kernel-features.h
+++ b/sysdeps/unix/sysv/linux/aarch64/kernel-features.h
@@ -27,3 +27,7 @@
    never issue it and glibc itself releases a dead thread's robust
    mutexes at thread exit.  */
 #undef __ASSUME_SET_ROBUST_LIST
+
+/* The Android app seccomp policy allows accept4 but traps accept, so
+   accept is implemented as accept4 with no flags.  */
+#undef __ASSUME_ACCEPT_SYSCALL
